sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#create): every new Instance is a ZFS clone of the Project's default Instance on its Node. A proof copy may be cloned on another Node that holds the default's current seed: it clones that Node's seed (docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-seed-on-each-ci-node). A clone's create ends when its thread is usable: the checkout, T3 and its registration (docs/reference/development-containers.md#a-clone-create-is-two-operations); its terminal projection admits `instance.complete` for the database, a nested fleet and the Processes (docs/cli/instance/complete.mmd). The create publishes the address beside the copy when the Route Nodes are free at its admission; else the completion publishes it. Built for the Nodes of the build list. The kind and its step names follow docs/cli/instance/create.mmd; the intent's `container.clone` marks a clone. The Project's first default Instance is container/create-default.mmd; when the charts move into place, it becomes the first-default branch of this chart.
  %% Four Swamp dispatches for a ready clone (2026-11-15): the copy step stages the release scripts from the Gateway's stage copy, so a clone runs no `input` or `clone-input` step; `clone-register` builds the create's result, so a ready clone skips `finish`. Each Swamp behavior step costs about 0.9 s of dispatch, an assert none. The step names `clone-container`, `clone-t3` and `clone-register` stay, in this order: Conn's create card reads them.
  %% Decided by the owner (2026-11-14) and the orchestrator (c3): the address is published during the create, beside the copy, in job `publication` (`clone-route-csr-<i>`, `clone-route`). The admission takes the Route Nodes only when it can and never waits for them: a Caddy-only publication shares them with removals and other such creates (at most eight on a Node), any other takes them alone; the Gateway frees them when `clone-route` ends, not at the create's end. Nodes held by another Route write leave the publication to the completion, as before.
